WEBVTT

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:02.440
What?

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:09.940
So he's awakened.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.470
Are you all right?

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.770
W-Was that El Ahda...?

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.470
And where did you come from?

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:45.040
If I said here, would you 
accept that explanation?

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.720
What in the world is—

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.790
You need to recover first.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:00.240
Where are we?

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.960
What's happening to me?

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.000
Calm down, Itsuki.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.860
How can you expect me to—

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.250
Is that the injury you suffered
against the Vol Dragon?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.250
I'm impressed you were able to 
fight the El Ahda in your state.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.010
You should be able to completely 
heal yourself using Monomates.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:30.000
I'm not dreaming.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.560
I am ARKS Intelligence's Commander Kasura.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.500
I'm Aika's superior.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:41.030
Would it be easier to understand 
if you thought of us as game NPCs?

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:42.790
NPCs?

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:43.960
In other words,

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.790
that would make Aika an NPC as well.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:47.540
What?

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.820
But you'll have to correct 
that thinking starting now.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:01:59.430
Tachibana Itsuki-kun,

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:01.100
do you understand?

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:04.180
We're not characters created for a game

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.590
or figments of your imagination.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:08.440
We exist in reality.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:09.740
What?

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.200
<i>PSO2</i> isn't a game.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:16.350
It's a world that actually exists.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.960
Welcome to Oracle, Tachibana Itsuki-kun.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.730
<b>Quest 09     Discharge Notice</b>

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:22.160
The disappearances and runaway car incidents

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.860
happening around you Earthlings

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:26.370
are the work of Darkers.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:27.960
Wait, wait.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:32.370
I'm confused enough already by your 
sudden declaration that <i>PSO2</i> is real.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:36.200
Now you're claiming Darkers are 
involved in the disappearances?

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:41.840
When Konoe Mika disappeared, 
you saw her being held here by Darkers.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:47.300
And when you were attacked by a Darker 
that appeared in the real world,

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.140
you used your power to defeat it.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.140
My power...

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:54.140
Put simply...

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:57.150
You unlocked your Photon Arts.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:01.320
By doing so, you were able to
directly come here,

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:05.820
to the world you recognize as the game world.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:08.820
In your battles against Darkers,

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:12.320
you should be able to exhibit a power
far greater than before.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.080
<i>I feel... powerful.</i>

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.830
I didn't think he'd be this strong.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:20.340
What?

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:25.520
<i>Wow.</i>

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:28.840
The Darkers need your power

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.560
as a vessel for Dark Falz.

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:33.350
A vessel?

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.180
To invade Earth,

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.360
Dark Falz requires a 
powerful vessel to inhabit.

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:44.820
Those with an aptitude for 
Photon Arts have that power.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:50.170
The Darkers have been searching for Earthlings
capable of using Photon Arts,

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:52.370
and abducting them to this world.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.370
Then Konoe-san...

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:59.530
Individuals you would call good 
at the game were likely targeted.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:04.380
Fortunately, Konoe Mika-san 
wasn't chosen to be a vessel.

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:08.460
Her latent Photon Arts must not 
have been very strong.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.390
But you're different.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:16.390
You appear to possess exceptionally 
strong Photon Arts for an Earthling.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:23.340
While secretly eliminating 
Darkers that appeared on Earth,

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:25.400
Aika was also watching you.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:27.150
Watching me?

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.410
Who is Dark Falz?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.910
Dark Falz

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:37.880
is the leader of the Darkers.

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.480
He's a threat to the universe.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.960
Itsuki-kun, we want your help.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.920
Your Photon Arts

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.780
will help us tremendously 
in defeating the Darkers.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.840
<i>This feels real.</i>

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:02.890
<i>The wind on my cheek, the temperature...</i>

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:10.980
<i>I'm definitely inside </i>PSO2<i> right now.</i>

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:14.580
They've been wiped out. Let's head back.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:16.500
No, wait.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:19.820
Let's look for them elsewhere 
and take them all out.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:23.900
Don't they say the best defense
is a good offense?

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:25.500
Leave it to me.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.260
Itsuki.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.260
Hey. Were you practicing this morning?

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:34.300
What's gotten into you?

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.710
You weren't at the dorm on Sunday,

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:39.020
and you've been going somewhere 
during all your breaks.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.480
Oh, you know. I've got a lot going on.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.400
The school festival is this week, too.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.020
I'm so busy!

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:46.960
You seem kind of hyper.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:47.770
Do I?

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:50.780
Good morning.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:52.750
Hey.

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:57.280
<i>They don't know anything, 
even though the Earth is in peril.</i>

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.780
Excuse me.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:01.790
S-Sure.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:04.790
Darkers again?

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:05.630
The bathroom.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.180
Don't try to hide it. I'll go with you.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:12.510
We fought yesterday and Sunday. 
You should rest.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:13.980
I'm fine.

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:17.510
With our consecutive victories, 
I'm in tip-top physical and mental shape.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:20.020
Who will do it if I don't?

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:23.660
The Darkers have been more 
active than ever lately.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:24.770
So I'll take them out.

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:28.770
It must be related to your exhibition 
of your flashy powers.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:29.270
What?

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:32.490
They gather around potential vessels.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:33.870
My commander said the same thing.

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:37.320
Wait. Are you—

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:38.300
I'm going to the bathroom!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.280
I can't believe he tried to 
follow her to the bathroom.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:42.610
It must be hard for Ai-Ai.

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:44.490
Tachibana is bad news.

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:45.640
I-It's not like that!

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:49.620
The Earth is peaceful again today.

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:56.040
Tachibana Itsuki-kun seems to be 
producing the results we expected.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:58.100
But the number of Darkers is increasing,

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:00.630
and they're focusing their attacks on Itsuki.

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:02.260
That's perfect.

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:07.710
At this rate, this could affect 
Itsuki's life on Earth.

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:10.710
If that's the choice he's made,

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.610
then it's a choice we must respect.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.980
Itsuki still doesn't understand real war.

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.370
If he keeps running out of control...

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:23.200
And keeping a firm grip on his leash 
is one of your responsibilities.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:26.870
<i>She totally left me behind!</i>

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:35.880
E-Everybody, welcome to Seiga 
Post-Night Festival...

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.540
Y-Yay.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:38.390
Yay!

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:40.220
Tachibana-kun?

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:41.390
What was that?

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:45.390
Masaya-kun and Mika told me to 
say this at the after party.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:46.640
Seriously?

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:50.910
They said I should seize the hearts 
of the students right from the start.

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:53.110
That would probably repel them instead.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:54.150
I-I know.

00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:56.870
B-But you'll be fine if you practice.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.910
Didn't you want to hold an after party?

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:00.910
Yeah.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:03.440
If I'm getting in the way, I'll leave.

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:04.540
I-It's fine.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.410
I'll try practicing in my room. Bye.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:09.920
Everybody!

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:14.000
Yay!

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:18.550
Now, then.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.120
Anyway...

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:21.300
Ai-Ai.

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:23.310
Have you seen Itsuki?

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:25.810
He just headed towards the roof.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:26.640
I see.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:28.810
He seemed to be in a hurry.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:31.310
<i>Did he go alone?!</i>

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:36.610
<b>[Oracle]</b> A fleet that exists in a dimension and universe different from Earth's. Through <i>PSO2</i>, those who possess an aptitude for Photon Arts can travel between the two worlds. Normal <i>PSO2</i> players control avatars created on ORACLE as their characters in the game without ever learning the truth that they act as ARKS.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:41.660
<b>[Photons]</b> Particles that exist in the atmosphere. On the ORACLE fleet, they are used on a daily basis for everything from lighting to powering 
the ARKS ships. Only those who can turn the photons in the atmosphere into energy without a catalyst are capable of fighting Darkers as ARKS.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:54.000
There's more.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:57.550
<i>Gotcha!</i>

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:43.620
Itsuki!

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:51.540
Hold still!

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:01.720
Are you okay?

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.450
My name is Xeno. Nice to meet you.

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:09.580
And this is Echo.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.660
You're hurt.

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.960
Hold on. I'll heal you right now.

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:20.300
They're coming.

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:22.290
Get up.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:23.470
Okay.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.100
I'll take you—

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:53.600
Damn, it wasn't deep enough.

00:12:56.870 --> 00:12:59.290
You surprised me by suddenly charging in.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:01.050
Wh-What was that?

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:03.220
Those were boosted enemies.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.600
Boosted enemies?

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:06.480
They're evolving.

00:13:07.420 --> 00:13:09.320
Looks like they're finished, too.

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.310
You two go on ahead.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:14.450
Sure.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:15.620
Got it.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.810
Suzuki-san, I...

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.100
Stay out of the fight from now on.

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:23.190
You're getting in the way.

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:24.200
What?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.800
<i>I'm a sorry mess...</i>

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:44.680
The school festival is in three days.

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:46.720
How is each class coming along?

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.440
I'll summarize and turn in—

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:49.720
I've got it right here.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.480
What is this? It's incredible.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:54.000
He's graphed out the progress 
of all the classes.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.730
Perfect. It's perfect.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:57.840
Vice President, when did you write this?

00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:59.940
I realized we needed it and whipped it up.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.360
Thank you. I appreciate it, Tachibana-kun.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:03.980
You can count on me.

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:06.740
You seem to be in awfully 
high spirits, Itsuki-kun.

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:09.560
Of course, Yu-chan. It's the school festival.

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:13.140
It's right in front of us. 
Our school festival is approaching.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:13.740
Yeah...

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:15.520
You're firing on all cylinders.

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:18.760
Of course. 
If you're short-staffed, let me know.

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:21.660
Vice President Tachibana Itsuki 
will take on all jobs.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:24.250
Then could you see how 
all the clubs are doing?

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.660
Got it.

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:27.680
Try not to push yourself.

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.840
We don't want you collapsing 
on the day of the festival.

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:32.260
That won't be a problem.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:36.520
By the way, where's Suzuki-san? 
I haven't seen her.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:40.400
What? Why would I know?

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:42.640
I'm off.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:54.910
<i>Stay out of the fight from now on.</i>

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:56.230
<i>You're getting in the way.</i>

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:10.680
They headed that way!

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:13.680
Let me handle it!

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:17.930
All right.

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:20.480
What's wrong? This isn't like you.

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:21.660
Sorry.

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:28.940
Hey, Itsuki. Marika and her friends 
were just looking for you.

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:30.660
Okay, got it.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:32.450
Still busy? Want to play?

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:35.080
Sorry, I'm seriously busy right now.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:35.950
Shucks.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:36.950
Suzuki-san?

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.340
We don't know what to do.

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:42.080
We need to take her measurements for her 
maid café uniform by the end of today.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.580
Ai-Ai's the only one left.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:47.010
Tachibana, what happened to Ai-Ai?

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:49.560
She hasn't come back to the dorm.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:51.050
Did she go home?

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:52.340
Have you heard anything?

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:53.590
Why would I know?

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:56.480
Because you're always together.

00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:57.230
Actually, that's—

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:58.990
You and Ai-Ai are a set.

00:15:58.990 --> 00:15:59.600
Yeah.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.840
I don't think she's coming back.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:05.640
Nothing.

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:07.730
She's dying? Ai-Ai is dying?

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:08.710
Don't say that!

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:10.730
And Tachibana, don't say 
weird stuff like that!

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:11.740
Sorry.

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:15.020
When we asked Ai-Ai to help at the maid café,

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:18.240
she didn't seem too 
enthusiastic at first, but...

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:20.500
Welcome back, Master.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.500
She really, really did her best.

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:25.980
She never expresses how she really feels.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:27.670
She can be kind of brusque.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.380
But she's actually really nice.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.010
And she has a strong sense of duty.

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:32.600
Hey.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.450
Did you get more coffee beans?

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:36.720
Oh, sorry!

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:40.020
I was going to get more once 
Ai-Ai got her measurements taken.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:41.420
I'll go.

00:16:41.420 --> 00:16:43.890
I haven't been helping the class much, anyway.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.520
Really? That would be great.

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:55.280
<i>Since Suzuki-san showed up, 
we have been around each other a lot.</i>

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:03.290
<i>Was she just watching me?</i>

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:05.290
I can't agree to this.

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:09.090
The Darkers are targeting the 
potential vessel Itsuki-kun.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:14.050
If it helps us predict their movements, 
we'll be able to respond quickly.

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:19.320
And you seem to be running on fumes.
 We could use him—

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:20.560
I can't agree to this.

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:26.200
He may have awakened his Photon Arts, 
but he's still only an Earthling.

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:31.500
Unlike us ARKS, he has no knowledge of Darkers
 and hasn't undergone formal combat training.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:36.950
But his Photon Arts are strong enough 
to draw that many Darkers to him.

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:41.830
Tachibana Itsuki has a life 
that's important to him.

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:44.580
I don't want to take that away from him.

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:49.170
Your priorities are out of order.

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:56.090
If Dark Falz invades Earth,
his life will be lost either way.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:57.840
I will stop him.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:01.850
Yikes.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:05.850
That's...

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:46.870
Run, Itsuki!

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:48.140
Suzuki-san!

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:51.020
I said run!

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:52.200
But...

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:54.650
Don't worry about it. This is my duty.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.150
Duty...

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:58.150
I will protect you.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:00.910
Run!

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:07.410
Isn't the school festival coming up?

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:10.790
<i>She never expresses how she really feels.</i>

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.700
<i>She can be kind of brusque.</i>

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:14.400
<i>But she's actually really nice.</i>

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:16.520
<i>And she has a strong sense of duty.</i>

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:29.810
I...tsuki...

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.320
I'll fight, too.

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:48.890
Did I get in your way?

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:49.930
Why?

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:54.400
Defeating the Darkers is the ARKS' duty.

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:57.400
You have no reason to fight,
so why did you?

00:20:58.660 --> 00:20:59.580
I do.

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:04.450
I can't just ignore you when 
you're fighting to protect me.

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:06.660
Let me fight with you.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.980
I won't get in your way anymore.

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:12.440
At least, I'll try not to.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:13.820
It's Aika.

00:21:14.630 --> 00:21:16.740
From now on, call me Aika.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:20.070
The other ARKS all call me that.

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:23.920
If you're the only one not calling me that,
it will affect our coordination.

00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:29.440
Thanks, Suzuki-san.

00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:30.480
It's Aika.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:32.460
Aika-san.

00:21:32.460 --> 00:21:33.740
Just Aika.

00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:37.850
Aika.

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:43.360
Being an ARKS is difficult. Prepare yourself.

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:44.960
I know.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:51.140
Can we still make it?

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:53.820
Your measurements for your maid café uniform!

00:21:53.820 --> 00:21:56.770
You haven't had them taken yet, right? 
You need to do that today.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:21:59.500
What?

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:03.130
You're right. That's an 
important duty as well.

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:08.120
I'll go with you. Let's hurry.

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:09.880
Got it.

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:41.940
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:41.940 --> 00:24:09.800
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:44.980
Things are settled for now, Aika.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:47.860
You look like things are going 
exactly as you planned, Commander.

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:49.540
That's not true at all.

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:52.320
Anyway, Aika, don't you 
have a mission on Earth?

00:23:52.320 --> 00:23:53.520
How do you know about that?

00:23:53.520 --> 00:23:56.410
I thought an Earth festival 
might provide some insights.

00:23:56.410 --> 00:23:58.160
Make sure you record it.

00:23:58.160 --> 00:23:59.400
I don't need to.

00:23:59.400 --> 00:24:00.730
Maid clothes, was it?

00:24:00.730 --> 00:24:02.500
I'm interested in seeing you 
dressed in those, as well.

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:03.280
Please stop.

00:24:03.280 --> 00:24:05.130
Things seemed to be going well at the end.

00:24:05.130 --> 00:24:07.600
If you showed that to Tachibana Itsuki-kun...

00:24:07.600 --> 00:24:09.800
Just how much are you 
spying on me, Commander?!
